            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for a beginner at the wheel, then the Mandarin for to pay for damage."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: bǎoxiǎn",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bǎoxiǎn — \"insurance\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "wǒ de chē yǒu bǎoxiǎn — My car is insured."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two third tones meet in this word: bǎo is said with a rising tone before xiǎn, and the spelling keeps both marks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bǎoxiǎn is built from bǎo 'to guard' and xiǎn 'danger', both inherited from Middle Chinese, pawX and xjemX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to guard' and 'safe' and the second 'danger': a guard against danger."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
